gomad: keep each retained success of one outcome signature as its own artifact
Two seeds of a target whose output does not depend on the seed complete
with one outcome signature. The success store was keyed by that
signature, so the second seed reused the first seed's artifact, the
campaign counted both, and inspect rejected the published record. The
success stores now use artifact.StoreKeyExecution: the first artifact
keeps the signature's directory, an existing artifact is reused only for
the same execution, and another execution is named by its campaign,
ordinal, seed and signature.

Reproduced with the built CLI on linux/arm64 (dev harness); evidence in
.flow/artifacts/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test/task-16/.

